3D viscous + gravity validation
===============================

This example validates `fix viscous` gravity handling in 3D Cartesian geometry
against the analytic ODE:

`dvz/dt = -nuE*vz + gz`, `dz/dt = vz`

Default run uses `nuE=0` (pure gravity through `fix viscous`), which is the
critical branch for geometry/projection correctness.

Files:
- `in.viscous_gravity3d`: SPARTA/OpenEdge input
- `source.1`: single-particle initial condition
- `droplet.species`: minimal species file
- `run_viscous_gravity_3d.py`: run + postprocess (CSV + PNG)

Run from repo root:

`python examples/test_viscous_gravity_3d/run_viscous_gravity_3d.py`

Outputs in `examples/test_viscous_gravity_3d/`:
- `dump.viscous_gravity3d`
- `viscous_gravity3d_validation.csv`
- `viscous_gravity3d_validation.png`
